1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,900
You're finally free,
Major Delgado.

2
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:03,500
Who are you going to interview

3
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:04,533
in Bolagos?

4
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:06,333
Are you going to interview
Miguel Delgado?

5
00:00:06,467 --> 00:00:07,900
It's hard to trust someone

6
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:10,233
you don't know very well.

7
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:11,700
I'm just worried about Jin Ho.

8
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,033
He still hasn't come home
since he said

9
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:15,267
he would keep an eye on Theresa.

10
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,300
He'll give Delgado a scene.

11
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:20,233
We'll give it to him.

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,067
I think I'm their target.

13
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,633
You won't be at peace

14
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:24,967
until you catch

15
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,633
the one who's after you.

16
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:28,700
As long as those syndicates
are there,

17
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:30,300
those drugs won't run out.

18
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:31,500
They can't win.

19
00:00:31,633 --> 00:00:33,833
Evil will prevail even more
if no one fights back.

20
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,900
You've only been free
for a few days,

21
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:36,933
and something like this
is happening.

22
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:38,533
I'm going to finish this fight.

23
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:40,100
We're here for you, Father.

24
00:00:40,233 --> 00:00:41,733
- Never say die?
- Never say die.

25
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,867
By the authority vested in me

26
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,200
and upon the directive of the
Regional Command,

27
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:48,367
I hereby reinstate you back
to service,

28
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:49,600
Major Miguel Delgado.

29
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:51,033
I see Delgado now.

30
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:51,933
Do you know Major?

31
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,167
Just passing by, Sir.

32
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,700
It's a good thing we met today.

33
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,333
Did you miss me?

34
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,233
You know...

35
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:39,100
I was like that before.

36
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:43,433
I couldn't eat, couldn't sleep,
I was just waiting for a reply,

37
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,000
But the ending was,
"nothing, zero, none."

38
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:49,233
What are you saying?

39
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:52,767
That's okay.

40
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,500
You will be able to find
someone else.

41
00:01:54,633 --> 00:01:55,533
My point is,

42
00:01:55,667 --> 00:01:58,167
maybe Jin Ho really wants
a woman,

43
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:00,100
so don't wait for his reply.

44
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:01,833
Are you crazy?

45
00:02:01,967 --> 00:02:03,367
I'm not in love with him.

46
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,867
I am just worried.

47
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,600
That's okay, Peter, come on.

48
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:07,733
Are you still shy around me?

49
00:02:07,867 --> 00:02:09,000
Don't hide it from me.

50
00:02:09,133 --> 00:02:10,233
Trust me.

51
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:12,167
It's only hard at first.

52
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:16,200
Hey, what's with you?

53
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:18,200
It's just a joke! It's a prank!

54
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:20,300
Come on, can I not
joke with you?

55
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:26,200
We're close.

56
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:27,500
Like that.

57
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:29,467
See?

58
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,667
Yes, I get it, I get it, okay?

59
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,500
My point is,
what I'm wondering is,

60
00:02:33,633 --> 00:02:34,900
why do you have to
keep your worries

61
00:02:35,033 --> 00:02:37,600
about Jin Ho to yourself?

62
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:39,767
You can also tell Joey.

63
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,500
No, I don't want to bother her.

64
00:02:41,633 --> 00:02:44,100
It's family time for her,
family time.

65
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:46,067
Oh, wow.

66
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,767
Then what,
will you be stressed alone?

67
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:51,133
You're something else,
you're a martyr.

68
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:52,900
You're really something.

69
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,400
Just eat.

70
00:02:54,533 --> 00:02:55,867
You talk too much.

71
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,067
Oh, here.

72
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,333
Oh, thank you.

73
00:02:58,467 --> 00:02:59,700
- Joey?
- Thank you, Ma'am.

74
00:02:59,833 --> 00:03:01,267
Mother.

75
00:03:02,733 --> 00:03:05,533
I noticed you and Andrew
are close.

76
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:07,633
You're not...

77
00:03:07,767 --> 00:03:08,833
are you not angry anymore?

78
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:10,867
You don't hate Boss Budol
anymore?

79
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:14,600
Oh, do you still want dessert?

80
00:03:14,733 --> 00:03:17,167
There's some more here,
just let me know.

81
00:03:17,567 --> 00:03:18,667
Joey...

82
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,867
You're so pretty now.

83
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:23,400
I didn't give birth to you
with deaf ears.

84
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:26,367
I know you heard me.

85
00:03:27,767 --> 00:03:29,200
Come on, Mom.

86
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:32,333
Your questions are so sudden.

87
00:03:33,667 --> 00:03:36,033
I was just asking questions.

88
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:40,233
So what now?

89
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:42,900
Are you close?

90
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:48,400
Maybe it's because I didn't know
him that well before

91
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:50,500
That's why I said
a lot of bad things

92
00:03:50,633 --> 00:03:52,267
about him.

93
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:55,433
But now that I know him,

94
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,367
he's kind.

95
00:04:01,067 --> 00:04:02,700
You're blushing, Joey.

96
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:03,700
What?

97
00:04:03,833 --> 00:04:04,867
- Yes.
- No.

98
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:12,100
Why are you teasing me, Mother?

99
00:04:14,467 --> 00:04:16,400
I'm just making a remark.

100
00:04:17,433 --> 00:04:20,000
What can I do if
you're feeling guilty, Joey?

101
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:24,500
Here.

102
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:26,667
Give him the dessert..

103
00:04:28,233 --> 00:04:30,567
so you two can be sweet.

104
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:35,400
- But, Mom...
- What?

105
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,667
Okay, but this means nothing,
okay?

106
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:42,033
-I'll just give it to him, okay?
-Of course.

107
00:04:42,167 --> 00:04:43,900
That really means nothing.

108
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:45,933
I'm on your side, Joey.

109
00:04:55,733 --> 00:04:57,867
Andrew, do you want
more dessert?

110
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:00,767
It's disgusting, it's ugly.
Too sweet.

111
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:02,533
Just be cool.

112
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,167
Oh, Andrew, do you want
a cold drink?

113
00:05:07,067 --> 00:05:08,767
Ah, that's ugly.

114
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:10,700
What should I say?

115
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:47,300
Andrew...

116
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:49,667
<i> Aren't you attracted to him?</i>

117
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,300
<i>Tall, handsome, with almond
eyes, and he smells good.</i>

118
00:05:53,433 --> 00:05:55,067
<i> Don't you like guys like that?</i>

119
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,233
<i> I don't look at him.</i>

120
00:05:57,367 --> 00:05:59,700
<i>That's why you should
look at him.</i>

121
00:05:59,833 --> 00:06:01,333
<i> You'll see.</i>

122
00:06:03,333 --> 00:06:05,400
<i> You're blushing, Joey.</i>

123
00:06:12,233 --> 00:06:13,833
Yes?

124
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,933
Joey...

125
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:28,933
Joey, hey! Joey!

126
00:06:29,933 --> 00:06:31,300
What?

127
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,833
What?

128
00:06:33,967 --> 00:06:37,000
I mean, why are you calling me?

129
00:06:38,033 --> 00:06:39,033
Calling you?

130
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:41,367
You're calling me, yes.

131
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:44,233
Oh it's because...

132
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:46,300
Because?

133
00:06:46,433 --> 00:06:48,300
Maybe you want dessert.

134
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,500
Are you mad?

135
00:06:51,633 --> 00:06:53,100
That's delicious.

136
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,033
Someone's calling.

137
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:58,933
Thank you.

138
00:07:13,067 --> 00:07:14,400
Come in.

139
00:07:16,367 --> 00:07:18,033
- Major Delgado.
- Sir.

140
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:23,400
This is the coordination letter

141
00:07:23,533 --> 00:07:25,467
and letter order you requested.

142
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,733
Thank you very much.

143
00:07:26,867 --> 00:07:29,033
I have also called you
to the Drug Enforcement

144
00:07:29,167 --> 00:07:33,000
Regional Office in the North
in the town of Belmora.

145
00:07:35,433 --> 00:07:38,633
Make a courtesy call
to their Regional Director.

146
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,233
Thank you very much, Sir,

147
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:42,133
for bringing me back
to this case.

148
00:07:42,267 --> 00:07:43,767
I thought about it carefully,

149
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:47,067
and you are still the best man
for the job.

150
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:50,633
especially since
you got a new lead.

151
00:07:51,633 --> 00:07:54,067
Just don't disappoint me,
Major, Delgado.

152
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,167
Thank you very much, Sir.

153
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:58,867
Please take care of my wife
and daughter.

154
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,633
Oh, don't worry.

155
00:08:01,367 --> 00:08:04,467
I have someoneto check on them
all the time.

156
00:08:05,033 --> 00:08:07,267
Be careful, Major Delgado.

157
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,300
Thank you, Sir.

158
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,467
<i>Major Miguel Delgado has
returned to service</i>

159
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,800
<i> after it was proven</i>

160
00:08:20,967 --> 00:08:23,367
<i>that he was not the real culprit
in the murder</i>

161
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,233
<i>of Major Staff Sergeant Ramon
Orbos.</i>

162
00:08:26,367 --> 00:08:28,000
<i> His name has also been cleared</i>

163
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,600
<i>of being a member
of the syndicate.</i>

164
00:08:30,733 --> 00:08:31,933
<i> According to Delgado,</i>

165
00:08:32,067 --> 00:08:34,367
<i> he is determined</i>

166
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,167
<i> not only to get justice</i>

167
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:37,667
<i> for what happened to him,</i>

168
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,200
<i>but to completely end the spread</i>

169
00:08:40,333 --> 00:08:42,033
<i>of illegal drugs in the country.</i>

170
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:44,000
Don't worry, Berdugo.

171
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,367
We've already prepared
everything for him.

172
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,633
Imagine,

173
00:08:49,767 --> 00:08:51,900
his first day in the service,

174
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,733
his last day in the world.

175
00:08:56,367 --> 00:08:58,733
How many times has he managed
to get past you?

176
00:08:58,867 --> 00:09:01,967
Make sure this doesn't
get out of hand.

177
00:09:02,567 --> 00:09:04,533
You can count on it, Berdugo.

178
00:09:08,433 --> 00:09:10,167
Sir.

179
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,833
Are you spying on me?

180
00:09:23,367 --> 00:09:26,567
No, Major, but I'm looking
for you.

181
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,667
Whatever you heard,

182
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,833
it can't get out.

183
00:09:33,967 --> 00:09:35,200
I know, but...

184
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,733
what's up in the North,

185
00:09:38,867 --> 00:09:40,833
in the town of Balmora?

186
00:09:41,433 --> 00:09:43,200
And wait, is this
still connected

187
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,400
to the syndicate
that set you up?

188
00:09:46,533 --> 00:09:49,200
And how did you get
a lead here, Major?

189
00:09:49,333 --> 00:09:51,467
You know I can't talk yet

190
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,633
because this is still under
investigation.

191
00:09:53,767 --> 00:09:55,700
Besides, this is just a lead.

192
00:09:56,567 --> 00:09:59,133
Don't worry, once I find out,
I'll tell you.

193
00:09:59,267 --> 00:10:01,900
Wait, do Joey and Ms. Clarissa

194
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:03,700
know you're going there?

195
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:06,000
They support me,

196
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,033
but there are still many things
they don't know.

197
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:12,067
So they can't know
what you heard,

198
00:10:12,533 --> 00:10:14,200
especially Joey.

199
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:18,967
Are you asking me to lie
to your daughter, Major?

200
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,233
No.

201
00:10:20,367 --> 00:10:21,700
What I'm saying is,

202
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,500
protect her...

203
00:10:23,633 --> 00:10:26,667
from things you know
will harm her.

204
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:32,100
Can't you just postpone
your trip until tomorrow?

205
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,900
Just leave tomorrow.

206
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:37,267
I want to be there
before the sun rises.

207
00:10:37,433 --> 00:10:39,400
Dad, you left this.

208
00:10:39,533 --> 00:10:41,700
Oh, I have to go.

209
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:47,200
You know, just think that...

210
00:10:47,333 --> 00:10:51,000
if I could get
the syndicate leader sooner,

211
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,533
I would be able
to get home here sooner.

212
00:10:54,567 --> 00:10:56,767
Dad, I'm going
to give you something.

213
00:10:58,267 --> 00:11:01,300
So you won't forget Mom and me.

214
00:11:01,733 --> 00:11:04,100
I really can't forget you.

215
00:11:04,233 --> 00:11:05,567
But...

216
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,767
this is cute, huh.

217
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,933
You take care of your Mom, okay?

218
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:11,067
Yes.

219
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,533
She might cry.

220
00:11:13,067 --> 00:11:15,067
She might miss me.

221
00:11:16,067 --> 00:11:19,933
Just make sure you're okay,

222
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:21,800
I'm okay too.

223
00:11:21,933 --> 00:11:23,333
Okay.

224
00:11:23,467 --> 00:11:24,633
- I'll go ahead.
- Dad...

225
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,967
Dad, where's your mission?

226
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,600
I'll tell you when I get there.

227
00:11:30,767 --> 00:11:32,233
Okay, I'll go ahead.

228
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:34,633
All right.

229
00:11:34,767 --> 00:11:36,900
Love you, Dad.
Be careful, okay?

230
00:11:42,667 --> 00:11:44,867
Okay, go inside, okay?

231
00:11:45,433 --> 00:11:46,433
- Go ahead.
- Are you sure?

232
00:11:46,567 --> 00:11:48,333
- I love you, Dad.
- I love you.

233
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:50,667
Be careful, okay?

234
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:52,967
Lock the door.

235
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,233
- Okay.
- The one upstairs, too.

236
00:11:54,367 --> 00:11:56,133
- All right.
- Love you.

237
00:11:56,267 --> 00:11:57,667
- Okay, Father.
- Love you. Be careful, okay?

238
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,233
Okay.

239
00:12:34,933 --> 00:12:36,000
Hey!

240
00:14:03,367 --> 00:14:05,000
Berdugo!

241
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:17,233
- Boss.
- Why only now?

242
00:14:17,367 --> 00:14:18,967
He passed by a lot of people.

243
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,433
<i> I only got the chance now.</i>

244
00:14:20,567 --> 00:14:21,967
Don't let it drag on.

245
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,533
Finish him.

246
00:14:23,667 --> 00:14:24,867
Sure, Boss.

247
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,433
You fool!

248
00:15:20,367 --> 00:15:22,267
Don't involve my family!

249
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:35,900
Kyle, start digging through
posts, news sites,

250
00:15:36,067 --> 00:15:37,267
vlogs, everything,

251
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,567
even private groups, okay?

252
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:42,167
Find out everything they're
investigating there

253
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:45,333
and everything related
to drugs in the North.

254
00:15:45,467 --> 00:15:46,800
Copy, Boss.

255
00:15:46,933 --> 00:15:51,333
Elai, contact all our sources
in the North.

256
00:15:51,467 --> 00:15:54,933
Everything, everything on
the ground related to drugs.

257
00:15:55,067 --> 00:15:56,767
- Okay.
- Okay?

258
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,267
We don't have a solid lead yet,

259
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:01,933
so we need to dig up
all the entry points.

260
00:16:02,067 --> 00:16:05,567
I'm sure something big is going
to happen in the next few days.

261
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,300
Where did you get
that information,

262
00:16:07,433 --> 00:16:09,333
and why are you
so anxious to know?

263
00:16:09,933 --> 00:16:11,267
My police contact.

264
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:14,667
It's better if you don't know
him for his safety.

265
00:16:25,767 --> 00:16:27,500
Do you want to save your family?

266
00:16:28,133 --> 00:16:30,033
You're going to die!

267
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:04,467
<i>You know, thank you so much
for not giving up on me.</i>

268
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,633
<i>- Oh! I told you, I didn't...
- No!</i>

269
00:17:06,767 --> 00:17:08,367
<i>- I promised, I promised.
- You're Dad.</i>

270
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:09,533
<i> I just slipped up!</i>

271
00:17:10,867 --> 00:17:13,133
<i>If I ever get back into the
service, I'll let you know.</i>

272
00:17:13,267 --> 00:17:14,833
<i> I know you don't want trouble,</i>

273
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,933
<i>but I can't abandon my duty
as a police officer.</i>

274
00:17:18,067 --> 00:17:20,800
<i>Evil prevails
when no one fights back.</i>

275
00:17:20,933 --> 00:17:22,100
<i> So I'm going back to service.</i>

276
00:17:22,233 --> 00:17:25,333
<i>Whatever your decision,
I'm on your side.</i>

277
00:17:38,433 --> 00:17:39,400
Chief.

278
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,467
Tell the others not to let
the media near

279
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,967
- until I tell them.
- Yes, Sir.

280
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:54,367
And take this
to Miguel's family.

281
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,367
Let them know what happened.

282
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:04,967
Joey...

283
00:18:05,433 --> 00:18:06,233
Mom.

284
00:18:06,367 --> 00:18:07,733
Where do you think your
dad is now?

285
00:18:08,333 --> 00:18:09,933
Hmm...

286
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:12,567
What? Do you want us
to call him again?

287
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,767
No need.

288
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:17,933
He might say we're too clingy,
right?

289
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:19,700
Hmm.

290
00:18:19,833 --> 00:18:20,833
Well, call him.

291
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:23,100
Okay, just one more.

292
00:18:23,233 --> 00:18:24,333
Mom misses him.

293
00:18:24,467 --> 00:18:25,700
Just one more,

294
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:27,700
so we know where he is.

295
00:18:33,633 --> 00:18:35,567
Who is that?

296
00:18:38,267 --> 00:18:39,367
Okay, all right, thank you.

297
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,667
Thank you, thank you.

298
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,167
What was that?

299
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:47,967
That's Argel, our correspondent.

300
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:51,333
There's a rumor that Godfather
is out in Timog,

301
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:55,733
and he has weakened
after the chaos at his party.

302
00:18:57,533 --> 00:19:00,633
I'm sure someone is waiting
to replace him.

303
00:19:01,233 --> 00:19:04,233
That's right, a new supplier
is coming in.

304
00:19:04,367 --> 00:19:05,900
Who is it? Berdugo?

305
00:19:06,033 --> 00:19:08,267
He hasn't given us a name yet.

306
00:19:08,933 --> 00:19:12,200
The boss sent me here
to give this to you.

307
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:26,733
This is Miguel's badge.

308
00:19:28,367 --> 00:19:30,100
Why do you have it?

309
00:19:31,667 --> 00:19:32,700
Why is it burned?

310
00:19:32,833 --> 00:19:35,100
We found Major's car.

311
00:19:35,233 --> 00:19:38,067
It was burning on the side of
Pacific Lateral Road.

312
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,533
He crashed into the barriers,

313
00:19:41,033 --> 00:19:42,667
which is why the car exploded.

314
00:19:47,667 --> 00:19:49,733
And Miguel?

315
00:19:50,433 --> 00:19:52,100
Where is Miguel?

316
00:19:54,733 --> 00:19:56,200
Cruz!

317
00:19:56,333 --> 00:19:58,200
Where is Miguel?

318
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:00,600
I'm sorry to say.

319
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:03,533
It looks like Major died
in the explosion.

320
00:20:08,633 --> 00:20:10,667
What? What is this?

321
00:20:12,333 --> 00:20:13,667
- Why?
- What's that?

322
00:20:15,633 --> 00:20:17,533
Our contact sent it.

323
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:20,733
They say a car exploded
on the Bolagos highway.

324
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:23,733
The victim looks like
a police officer.

325
00:20:24,567 --> 00:20:26,000
Let me see.

326
00:20:29,867 --> 00:20:31,267
Let's go there.

327
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:36,133
No, that's not true.

328
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:37,700
That can't be true.

329
00:20:37,833 --> 00:20:39,900
My husband just left!

330
00:20:40,033 --> 00:20:42,233
That's right, Dad just left.

331
00:20:43,967 --> 00:20:44,800
That can't be.

332
00:20:44,933 --> 00:20:47,367
Nothing bad happened
to my husband.

333
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:50,100
That can't be happening.

334
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:55,867
Mom...

335
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:01,467
No, that can't be happening.

336
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:03,067
No, no, no.

337
00:21:03,667 --> 00:21:05,433
Dad just left.

338
00:21:13,067 --> 00:21:14,667
Sir...

339
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,000
I want to see Dad.

340
00:21:16,133 --> 00:21:17,900
Where is Dad?
I want to go to him.

341
00:21:18,033 --> 00:21:19,967
Please, I'm begging you.

342
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:22,933
Take us to Dad, please!

343
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:39,467
An officer of the Bolagos Police

344
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,800
is suspected
of having died here.

345
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,200
The plate number
and the personal effects

346
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:43,933
that were recovered
have been confirmed.

347
00:21:44,067 --> 00:21:45,500
Everything belongs to Miguel.

348
00:21:45,633 --> 00:21:47,400
Can I see him first?

349
00:21:47,533 --> 00:21:49,833
It's not a good idea
to see your father like this.

350
00:21:49,967 --> 00:21:51,067
Poor Delgado.

351
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,367
He got what he deserved.

352
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:55,300
Do you really believe
that Dad is dead?

353
00:21:55,433 --> 00:21:57,600
Don't you want to hope
that he's still alive?

354
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:58,567
All his battles

355
00:21:58,700 --> 00:21:59,767
were for the good.

356
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:01,833
His story shouldn't end
like this.

357
00:22:01,967 --> 00:22:03,567
That's why I don't believe it.

358
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,833
I have a really strong feeling
that Dad is still alive.

359
00:22:05,967 --> 00:22:07,000
Where are they
taking the remains?

360
00:22:07,133 --> 00:22:08,400
To the crime lab for autopsy.

361
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:09,533
While there is no proof yet,

362
00:22:09,667 --> 00:22:11,833
I believe Dad is still alive.
